# Committed baseline of the DNA hashes the fleet is contracted to run.
#
# Format: <role>=<uhC0k… DNA hash>, one per line, blank lines and `#` comments
# ignored. `role` matches the happ.yaml role name (elohim/workdir/happ.yaml),
# not the DNA directory name (node-registry dir -> node_registry role).
#
# Read and enforced by scripts/ci/dna-hash-guard.sh in the "DNA Hash Guard" stage
# of elohim/holochain/dna/Jenkinsfile: a build whose packed DNA hash diverges
# from this file FAILS unless its commit is tagged [dna:migrate] — a moved
# integrity hash orphans the fleet's DHT data and re-keys every node, so it is a
# declared migration, never a side effect.
#
# CONTRACT: these are PACKED-DNA hashes (`hc dna hash workdir/<role>.dna`), NOT the
# hashes a conductor reports as installed. The installed DnaHash folds in the happ.yaml
# role modifiers (four roles carry `properties: {progenitor_pubkey: null}`; infrastructure
# carries `properties: null` and is the only role where the two coincide). Never compare
# this file against `/version`, `app_info`, or storage's "installed" log lines — compare
# it only against the pipeline's own `DNA-HASH <role> <hash>` lines. The invariant it
# guards is byte-identity of the integrity zomes between builds.
#
# 2026-09-02 — values are elohim-holochain #1420's packed hashes, byte-identical to #1414
# (the last pre-incident build). The commit that set them (7d9096263) was labelled
# [dna:migrate] on a MISREADING: the previous baseline held INSTALLED hashes, which can
# never match packed ones for the four roles with properties, so the guard fired on a
# comparison that was wrong by construction. No migration occurred — the fleet re-genesised
# onto the same five DNA hashes it had run since July. Escalation atom (CORRECTION 2):
#   genesis/data/timeline/backlog/alpha-conductor-crash-loop-after-wave4-roll-and-moved-dna-hashes.md
# 2026-09-03 — HOLOCHAIN 0.7 MIGRATION (the first real one). Values are elohim-holochain #1424's
# packed hashes: hdk 0.7 / hdi 0.8 integrity zomes on the holochain-0.7.0 line. The commit that moved
# the fleet is tagged [dna:migrate] (a78904105 on dev, guide
# genesis/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-02-holochain-0-7-upgrade-guide.md; operator runbook
# 2026-09-03-holochain-0-7-fleet-cutover-runbook.md). Every 0.6 chain is orphaned by design — the
# fleet is wiped clean and re-genesised onto these five (operator authorization 2026-09-03).
